    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Jackson Merrill** (74.47) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.04) headlining the lineup as our most viable options for offensive production. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a strong matchup against Elder and a prime spot in the two-hole, bolstered by a 13% platoon efficiency gain. **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) also presents as a top-tier play; while the raw base projection was moderate, a favorable clash against a soft 7.04 xERA arm combined with his leadoff role makes him a high-floor target. Meanwhile, **Drake Baldwin** (68.13) provides sneaky value at catcher, as his elite xwOBA metrics and leadoff positioning negate the traditional lack of production expected from the position.\n\nConversely, we are navigating a high-risk landscape with our lower-tier starters. **Luis Robert Jr.** (40.13) and **Sam Antonacci** (47.20) are both facing elite-level arms with xERAs near or below 3.00, significantly suppressing their efficiency scores. While we prioritize speed, **Luis Robert Jr.** is fighting a brutal 19% penalty against the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill set, making him a candidate for early removal if the game script turns negative. On the bench, **Curtis Mead** (52.30) was the most difficult exclusion; he projected well due to a significant park-adjusted ceiling, but he ultimately ceded his spot to **Coby Mayo** (53.73), whose superior platoon efficiency and slightly more favorable underlying projections provided a marginal but necessary edge in our quest to protect game caps. We must remain cautious of the volatility surrounding **Gunnar Henderson** (54.67), whose score is tethered to a difficult matchup against Tolle, and we will monitor the situation closely to ensure our SB targets like **Nasim Nunez** (56.05) are not wasted against elite batteries.",
